        }

        .logo img {
            height: 90px;
            width: auto;
            object-fit: contain;
        }

        .nav-links {
            display: flex;
            gap: 30px;
        }

        .nav-links a {
            color: #08123B;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 600;
            transition: .3s;
        }

        .nav-links a:hover {
            color: #FF532E;
        }

        .blog-hero {
            background: #08123B;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 80px 20px;
        }

        .blog-hero span {
            color: #FF532E;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .blog-hero h1 {
            font-size: 48px;
            margin-top: 15px;
        }

        .blog-container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 60px auto;
            padding: 0 25px;
        }

        .blog-image {
            width: 100%;
            max-height: 480px;
            object-fit: cover;
            border-radius: 18px;
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .blog-content h2 {
            font-size: 30px;
            margin: 35px 0 15px;
        }

        .blog-content p {
            font-size: 17px;
            line-height: 1.9;
            color: #555;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .blog-content ul {
            margin: 20px 0 30px 25px;
        }

        .blog-content li {
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            color: #555;
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        .back-btn {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 8px;
            padding: 13px 22px;
            background: #FF532E;
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-weight: 600;
            margin-top: 25px;
            transition: .3s;
        }

        .back-btn:hover {
            transform: translateY(-3px);
        }

        footer {
            background: #08123B;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 30px 20px;
            margin-top: 70px;
        }

        footer p {
            color: #ccc;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        footer a {
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            margin: 0 10px;
        }

        footer a:hover {
            color: #FF532E;
        }

        @media(max-width: 768px) {

            .navbar {
                padding: 0 20px;
            }

            .nav-links {
                display: none;
            }

            .blog-hero h1 {
                font-size: 34px;
            }

        }

    </style>

</head>

<body>

    <nav class="navbar">

        <a href="/" class="logo">

            <img
                src="/images/logo.png"
                alt="RideWave"
            >

        </a>


        <div class="nav-links">

            <a href="/">Home</a>

            <a href="/#rentals">
                Rentals
            </a>

            <a href="/teams">
                Teams
            </a>

            <a href="/#faq">
                FAQ
            </a>

            <a href="/blog">
                Clips
            </a>

            <a href="/contact">
                Contact
            </a>

        </div>

    </nav>


    <section class="blog-hero">

        <span>
            30 Aug 2026
        </span>

        <h1>
            Essential Things to Check Before Renting
        </h1>

    </section>


    <main class="blog-container">

        <img
            src="/images/blog-3.0.png"
            alt="Car Rental Inspection"
            class="blog-image"
        >


        <div class="blog-content">

            <p>
                Before driving away in a rental car, it is important
                to inspect the vehicle and understand the rental
                agreement. A few simple checks can help prevent
                unexpected problems later.
            </p>


            <h2>1. Check the Exterior</h2>

            <p>
                Walk around the vehicle and inspect the body for
                scratches, dents, paint damage, broken lights, or
                cracked mirrors.
            </p>


            <h2>2. Check the Interior</h2>

            <p>
                Check the seats, dashboard, air conditioning,
                infotainment system, windows, mirrors, and other
                interior features.
            </p>


            <h2>3. Check the Fuel Level</h2>

            <p>
                Confirm the fuel level before starting your journey.
                Make sure you understand the company's fuel policy
                and return requirements.
            </p>


            <h2>4. Check the Documents</h2>

            <p>
                Make sure the required rental documents and vehicle
                papers are available. Keep your driving licence and
                other required identification with you.
            </p>


            <h2>5. Understand the Insurance</h2>

            <p>
                Before accepting the vehicle, understand what is
                covered by the rental protection or insurance and
                whether any additional charges may apply.
            </p>


            <h2>6. Check the Rental Terms</h2>

            <p>
                Carefully review mileage limits, cancellation rules,
                late-return charges, security deposits, fuel policy,
                and other important rental conditions.
            </p>


            <h2>7. Take Photos</h2>

            <p>
                Taking clear photos or videos of the vehicle before
                starting your rental can help document its condition
                at the time of pickup.
            </p>


            <h2>Final Checklist</h2>

            <ul>

                <li>✓ Exterior condition</li>

                <li>✓ Interior condition</li>

                <li>✓ Fuel level</li>

                <li>✓ Vehicle documents</li>

                <li>✓ Insurance details</li>

                <li>✓ Rental agreement</li>

                <li>✓ Existing damage</li>

            </ul>


            <p>
                Taking a few minutes to complete these checks can make
                your RideWave rental experience smoother and more
                stress-free.
            </p>


            <a
                href="/blog"
                class="back-btn"
            >

                <i class="bx bx-left-arrow-alt"></i>

                Back to Clips

            </a>

        </div>

    </main>


